entries.text:
{w=0.7}"I'll repeat what I did. I was the first to leave the attic, and I went to the second floor. I spent several minutes there, during which I heard the elevator once."{w}

"Then, Erina's voice echoed to me, but it was very muddled. All I recognized was "Don't lie! It can only be you. You killed them.""{w}

"I ran down the staircase and found her dead. I didn't see or hear anyone else, so I ran back up to find you all."

entries.new:
{w=0.7}「我把自己做过的事再说一遍。我第一个离开阁楼，去了二楼。在那里待了几分钟，其间听到过一次电梯的声音。」{w}

「后来，Erina 的声音传到我耳边，但十分模糊。我只听清了『别撒谎！只可能是你。是你杀了他们。』」

「我顺着楼梯跑下去，发现她已经死了。我没看见也没听见其他人，于是又跑上来找你们。」

entries.text:
{w=0.4}"Right. He found me first since I was on the third floor. I left the attic later than him and walked through the floors until I stayed on the third."{w}

"I just wanted to be alone for a bit, but I didn't feel like staying put somewhere. However, I ended up spending the most time on the third floor, where I heard the elevator. I spent some time in the offices and some outside."{w}

"Some minutes later, Atsuki came running from below."

entries.new:
{w=0.4}「对。我在三楼，所以他先找到了我。我比他晚离开阁楼，一路走过几层，最后停在了三楼。」{w}

「我只是想一个人待一会儿，又不想一直守在同一个地方。结果三楼成了我待得最久的地方，我就是在那里听见电梯的。我先在办公室里待了一阵，又到外面待了一阵。」{w}

「几分钟后，Atsuki 从楼下跑了上来。」

entries.text:
{w=0.4}"I don't think accomplices came into play, because it seems like Erina was killed after she accused someone of being the culprit. However, since you and Atsuki know each other, he could be covering for you."{w}

"Also, if you took the elevator with Erina and Isla, you could've used it to reach the third floor after killing her and sent it back to the crystal floor from there."{w}

"Remember when we sent it from the sixth floor to the crystal floor? We heard no noise. If at that point, Atsuki was already running down the staircase, he might not have heard you. Did you check the elevator when you found Erina?"

entries.new:
{w=0.4}「我不认为有共犯。Erina 是在指认凶手之后才被杀的。不过，你和 Atsuki 彼此认识，他有可能在替你遮掩。」{w}

「还有，如果你和 Erina、Isla 一起乘了电梯，你完全可以在杀了她之后坐电梯去三楼，再把电梯送回水晶层。」{w}

「还记得我们从六楼把电梯送到水晶层那回吗？我们什么都没听见。如果那时 Atsuki 已经在往楼下跑，他也许就听不到你的动静。你发现 Erina 的时候，检查过电梯吗？」

entries.text:
{w=0.4}"Precisely. That's where I was the entire time."{w}

"In the attic, I spent a few minutes in one of the bedrooms with Akaro. Soon, I noticed some people had left, so I checked to see who remained."{w}

"I was a bit angry people were entering and leaving the attic without my consent, so I went to find the people who had left."{w}

"However, I reached the fifth floor and recalled the two dead bodies. Most importantly, that a killer was around. That's what made me stop."{w}

"I had thousands of things to think about, and that's what I did. I went over the incident to see if there was any conclusion I could get to, but ultimately, I didn't move from there. I heard the elevator once, which was the only sound that reached my ears until you guys came."

entries.new:
{w=0.4}「正是。我一直在那里。」{w}

「在阁楼时，我和 Akaro 在其中一个房间里待了几分钟。不久我发觉有人离开了，就去确认还剩哪些人。」{w}

「有人不经我允许就在阁楼里进进出出，我有些恼火，便去找那些离开的人。」{w}

「可走到五楼，我又想起了那两具尸体，尤其是——凶手还在附近。我因此停下了脚步。」{w}

「我要想的事太多了，就站在那里想。我把整件事从头到尾过了一遍，看能不能得出什么结论，但最终一步也没有挪。其间我听到过一次电梯的声音，直到你们赶来，那是我耳朵里唯一的响动。」

entries.text:
{w=0.4}"That's fine by me, and I can confirm it: he's telling the truth."{w}

"The reason why I stayed on the fourth floor was different from everyone else's. It was because I quickly began to hear noise coming from the floor above me. More specifically, footsteps that I now know belonged to Katei."{w}

"I paid attention to see if there was anything I could figure out from them, but they simply kept going in circles, so it gave the impression that whoever was walking above me was either lost in thought or fairly nervous."{w}

"For most of the time, the sound of footsteps came directly from the third partition. However, during the last few minutes, they left it and started to come from outside the offices."{w}

"When I heard the elevator, I thought the person above me would come down. That never happened, though, and the footsteps never ceased. There was no time for Katei to do anything."

entries.new:
{w=0.4}「我没意见，而且我可以作证：他说的是实话。」{w}

「我留在四楼的理由和各位不同。因为我很快就听见楼上传来动静，准确地说，是脚步声——现在我知道那是 Katei 的。」{w}

「我留心去听，想从中听出些什么，可那脚步只是在原地打转，给人的感觉是，楼上那个人不是在出神，就是相当紧张。」{w}

「大部分时间里，脚步声都直接从第三个隔间那边传来。不过在最后几分钟，它离开了那里，开始从办公室外传来。」{w}

「听到电梯时，我以为楼上的人会下来。可那人始终没下来，脚步声也一直没停。Katei 根本没有时间做别的事。」

